Fillet corner treatment for exact tangencies (the "tangent pinch").

What it fixes
  A fillet whose spine ends where one of its supports is exactly tangent
  to a third, planar face — a cylindrical boss standing on a plate
  exactly as wide as its diameter. The fillet's width there is capped at
  R/|cos t| from the boss axis, which equals R exactly at the tangency,
  so the correct toroidal face pinches to a point where its inner
  contact circle touches the grazing plane. The generic n-corner code
  (PerformMoreThreeCorner) instead fills the corner with a GeomPlate
  patch that self-intersects along the plate boundary, swallows most of
  the fillet volume, and reports IsDone() == true: on a 20 x 40 x 10
  plate with a tangent r=10 boss and a 2 mm fillet the result carried an
  unorientable B-spline face, a self-intersecting wire, breached the
  bounding box by 0.23 mm, and added 5.17 mm^3 of fillet where the
  correct answer adds ~47.5.

  The new ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTangentPinch, dispatched from
  PerformFilletOnVertex before the generic treatments, builds the exact
  answer: each stripe keeps its analytic KPart torus, extended along the
  tangent support to the pinch apex; each stripe end is closed by the
  exact intersection curve of that torus with the grazing face; and when
  only one stripe end reaches the vertex, the extended face and the
  support meet along the tangent generator, added as a new curve, with
  the consumed spine edge removed the way the singular-corner code does.
  Vertices that are not of this exact form are left to the existing
  treatments untouched.

How it was measured
  BRepCheck_Analyzer valid, watertight welded mesh (0 open edges),
  bounding box exact, on both trigger shapes:
  - box(20,40,10) + tangent cylinder(r10,h25), blend 2: volume
    14326.55 mm^3 = plain union 14279.05 + 47.50 of fillet.
  - the parcad retainer (59.49 mm plate with a flush disc, Fusion 360
    reference part): volume 143829.66 mm^3 against the reference
    B-rep's 143825.6, with every downstream boolean of the part intact.
  Clearance sweep around the tangency (1e-9 .. 2.001 mm) stays valid
  and watertight; the previously-failing 1e-9 and 1e-7 rows now build.

Upstream status
  Not yet offered upstream (github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT).
